     kkyyuuaa aabboouutt — Shows detailed authors, license, and version information

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     kkyyuuaa aabboouutt [_a_u_t_h_o_r_s | _l_i_c_e_n_s_e | _v_e_r_s_i_o_n]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ‘about’ command provides generic information about the kyua(1) tool.
     In the default synopsis form (no arguments), the information printed in‐
     cludes:

     1.   The name of the package, which is ‘kyua’.

     2.   The version number, which is ‘0.13’.

     3.   License information.

     4.   Authors information.

     5.   A link to the project web site.

     You can customize the information printed by this command by specifying
     the desired topic as the single argument to the command.  This can be one
     of:

     _a_u_t_h_o_r_s    Displays the list of authors and contributors only.

     _l_i_c_e_n_s_e    Displays the license information and the list of copyrights.

     _v_e_r_s_i_o_n    Displays the package name and the version number in a format
                that is compatible with the output of GNU tools that support a
                ----vveerrssiioonn flag.  Use this whenever you have to query the ver‐
                sion number of the package.

FFIILLEESS
     The following files are read by the kkyyuuaa aabboouutt command:

     /usr/share/doc/kyua/AUTHORS
         List of authors (aka copyright holders).

     /usr/share/doc/kyua/CONTRIBUTORS
         List of contributors (aka individuals that have contributed to the
         project).

     /usr/share/doc/kyua/LICENSE
         License information.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The kkyyuuaa aabboouutt command always returns 0.

     Additional exit codes may be returned as described in kyua(1).

